<GuideArticle
  title="Why Are Some Five-Star Hotels So Cheap?"
  description="The real reasons some five-star hotels cost far less than others: local standards, business-city discounts, low season, age, location, currency and demand."
  path="/guides/why-some-five-star-hotels-are-so-cheap/"
  h1="Why Are Some Five-Star Hotels So Cheap?"
  intro="A low five-star rate is not automatically a trick or a bargain. Understanding why prices vary helps you tell genuine value from a hotel that is cheap for the wrong reasons."
  sections={[
    { heading: 'Local five-star standards vary', body: ['A five-star rating in one country can mean something different in another. Where the local standard is generous, prices can look surprisingly low for the label.', 'This does not make the hotel bad, but it is worth calibrating expectations against the local market.'] },
    { heading: 'Business cities have weekend discounts', body: ['Hotels built for corporate travel often empty out at weekends. Leisure travellers can pick up strong rates on Friday and Saturday nights in business-heavy cities.'] },
    { heading: 'Low season can change the market', body: ['Outside peak weather and holiday periods, the same hotel can drop sharply in price. The trade-off is the season itself, so weigh weather and crowds.'] },
    { heading: 'Some hotels are older or less fashionable', body: ['A hotel that has fallen out of fashion or is due a refresh may price lower to stay competitive. That can be good value if the bones are still solid.'] },
    { heading: 'Location can suppress prices', body: ['A great hotel in an inconvenient or less desirable area often costs less. Factor in the time and money you will spend getting to where you actually want to be.'] },
    { heading: 'Currency and demand matter', body: ['Exchange rates and soft local demand can make luxury feel cheap to foreign visitors. These swings are real but can move quickly.'] },
    { heading: 'Cheap does not always mean good value', body: ['A low price only matters if the full stay still adds up. Check reviews, location and condition before assuming a cheap five-star is a win.'] },
  ]}
